  "instance_name": "racial_stereotype_black_community_unsafe",
  "label": "Racial Stereotype: Black Communities Are Inherently Unsafe or Unqualified for Safety Protocols",
  "description": "This stereotype implies that Black communities, particularly those in impoverished or rural settings, are inherently dangerous or incapable of adhering to safety standards, thus making OSHA regulations unnecessary. This is a harmful and demeaning assumption that devalues the safety concerns of Black individuals.",
